238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Urban parking is a growing real-world challenge, especially in high-traffic cities where static pricing fails to reflect real-time demand and availability. This leads to inefficient space usage, increased congestion, and user frustration.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Our project addresses this problem by designing a dynamic pricing system for urban parking lots. Using real-time data streams and economic logic, we aim to adjust parking prices in response to demand, congestion, and competitor behavior.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We implement this solution using Pathway, a real-time data processing framework, to simulate and test our pricing models on live-streamed parking data.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
